yoyo config get modle now says the key isn't a settable config key and suggests model, instead of claiming it's sitting at its default. Build, test, clippy and fmt all pass, and it's committed as cfb7e95a.

Before and after (run from an empty temp dir with HOME pointed there, so no config file was loaded):

| Command | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| config get modle | modle is not set in config file (using default) | modle is not a settable config key, and it is not set in the config file (did you mean model?), followed by the list of settable keys |
| config get zzzzqqq | not run before the change | same refusal, with no suggestion |
| config get model | model is not set in config file (using default) | unchanged, byte for byte |

All three still exit 0, as the task scoped. I added a comment to #982 noting that the config get arm now prints a refusal but still exits 0.

What changed:
• A new function in src/commands_config.rs, config_get_unknown_key_message(key, known), makes the decision. It only runs when the key isn't in the config file, and its list of known keys comes from SETTABLE_KEYS. For the suggestion it reuses the existing commands::closest_match (edit distance up to 2) rather than adding a second one. The output has no glyphs.
• **Wording:** the message says "not a *settable* config key", not "not a config key". The config file also accepts keys that aren't in `SETTABLE_KEYS` (`base_url, context_window, sub_agent_model`, …), and there's no list of all of them. The stronger wording would wrongly call those real, unset keys invalid. Keys written as `permissions.*` don't need handling: the parser ignores section headers, so config get never sees dotted keys.
• Tests cover four cases: modle gets a suggestion; zzzzqqq gets none and the words "using default" don't appear; every key in SETTABLE_KEYS returns None, so keys added later are covered automatically; and the output is plain ASCII.
• Positive control: I made the function always return None (marked NEUTERED), ran it as one command, and restored it. Three tests failed by name and the every-key test stayed green. After restoring, all four passed.

Where I went past or fell short of the task:
• **Two extra files.** The task said `commands_config.rs` only, but that file sits in the size gate's 50-line overshoot band; it's now 2042 lines against a cap of 2050. So the tests went in a new src/commands_config_get_tests.rs, declared in src/main.rs the same way the existing tools_*_tests files are. A #[path] declaration didn't satisfy the orphan-module gate.
• **No unit test for the model output.** I didn't add a full-string `assert_eq!` on the "(using default)" line. That line is printed inside `handle_config_get` and nothing returns it as a string. It's covered by the every-key-returns-None test plus the before/after run above.
• **No doc updates.** Nothing under `docs/src` or `README.md` describes `config get` output.
